# Pull request copy

When creating or updating a PR:

1. **Title** — Conventional Commits: `type(scope): description` (scope optional). Prefer `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `perf`, `ci`. Sentence case after the colon; no trailing period.
2. **Body** — Short and concrete: what changed and why. Skip filler Summary/Test plan theater unless the change needs a real checklist. Before finalizing, read and apply the `unslop` skill so the prose has no AI tells.
3. **Squash merge message** — Same title and body as the PR (not the branch commit history).

```text
# ✅ GOOD
feat(consumers): pause lag poll while the drawer is open

Stop the consumers query while the detail drawer is open so the
table does not keep refreshing under the panel.

# ❌ BAD
Update consumers page

## Summary
- Improved the overall user experience by enhancing polling behavior
- Ensured a more seamless interaction when viewing details
```
